{"type":"message","id":"3319c941","parentId":"a7a10509","timestamp":"2026-04-14T11:22:28.605Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking if I updated the session. This is a bit odd - they might be asking about something that happened previously. Let me check what they mean. In Chinese, \"你更新session了吗\" means \"Did you update the session?\"\n\nThis could mean:\n1. They're asking if I updated/refreshed my session context\n2. They might be referring to something specific from a previous conversation\n\nSince this is a new session (started via /new or /reset), I should greet them and also clarify what they mean. They might be referring to some prior conversation about updating something.\n\nLet me respond in a friendly way asking for clarification about what they mean.\n","thinkingSignature":"6ae23bf3dcebdd476083ea1df8f9a813ab36cfc839c89f63f2bbaeebf54c984d"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n频哥，我每次对话都是从头开始的，所以你说的\"更新session\"是指什么呢？是之前我们在聊什么事情吗？你说说看，我来帮你继续 😊"}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":264,"output":167,"cacheRead":26496,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":26927,"cost":{"input":0.0000792,"output":0.0002004,"cacheRead":0.00158976,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00186936}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1776165697532,"responseId":"062d5642689478b7f88eb523793e3d64"}}
